# speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite
"Now is not the time for accusations, both of you."

The tension lingers in the air as Poet frowns at being dismissed. King nods in acknowledgement and moves on, keeping her composure.

# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"Nevertheless. You are here and I am telling you now."

Soldier cuts in, 

# speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite
"Yes, but why are you? Telling us that is?"

King sighs again, something she had done a lot during their conversation.

# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"Aside from the fact that I believe you both could provide valuable insight as advisors-"

This time, Soldier is the one to cut King off.

# speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite
"I belong on the battlefield."

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
 "I belong with and to the people." Poet echoes.

# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"You belong here with me", King says firmly. 

The other two open their mouths to speak, but King carries on. 

# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"Most especially if our suspicions are correct and the people behind this were behind that night as well."

A stiff silence settles over the room, neither Soldier nor Poet making any move to contradict.


